#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# std_dev

#% text
# `std_dev(xs)` gives the sample standard deviation of the list of values `xs`.

#% text
# `std_dev(d)` gives the standard deviation of the distribution `d`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The sample standard deviation is `sqrt(variance(xs))`, with the divisor n - 1.

#% item
# Exact values give an exact result, machine reals a machine real.

#% item
# For a list of rows, the standard deviation is taken column by column.

#% item
# A list needs at least two elements.

#% item
# A distribution without a finite variance gives `failure(undefined, std_dev, d)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The standard deviation of four integers:

#% cell
std_dev([1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= (1/3)*15^(1/2)

#% text
# Of machine reals:

#% cell
std_dev([2.0, 4.0, 4.0, 4.0, 5.0, 5.0, 7.0, 9.0])
#% output
#= 2.138089935299395

#% text
# Of a distribution:

#% cell
std_dev(normal_distribution(mu, sigma))
#% output
#= sigma

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Column by column:

#% cell
std_dev([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 9]])
#% output
#= [2, 13^(1/2)]

#% text
# Of several distributions:

#% cell
[std_dev(exponential_distribution(l)), std_dev(poisson_distribution(4)), std_dev(uniform_distribution([0, 1]))]
#% output
#= [l^-1, 2, (1/6)*3^(1/2)]

#% text
# Of symbols:

#% cell
std_dev([a, b])
#% output
#= ((a + (-1/2)*(a + b))^2 + (b + (-1/2)*(a + b))^2)^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The spread of simulated data, close to the 3 it was drawn with:

#% cell
seed(2); std_dev(random_variate(normal_distribution(0, 3), 10^4))
#% output
#= 3.0279636615805514

#% text
# The standard error of a mean, std_dev/sqrt(n):

#% cell
seed(3); xs = random_real([0, 1], 400); [mean(xs), std_dev(xs)/sqrt(400)]
#% output
#= [0.4872697517955293, 0.014293262934954927]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The square is the variance:

#% cell
std_dev([1, 2, 3, 4])^2 == variance([1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= true

#% text
# With the divisor n instead of n - 1, from the second central moment:

#% cell
sqrt(central_moment([1, 2, 3, 4], 2))
#% output
#= (1/2)*5^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# One value has no sample standard deviation:

#% cell
std_dev([5])
#% output
#! failure(argument, std_dev, "the list needs at least two elements")

#% text
# A distribution with infinite variance:

#% cell
std_dev(student_t_distribution(1))
#% output
#! failure(undefined, std_dev, student_t_distribution(1))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `variance`, `mean`, `median`, `central_moment`, `quantile`
